**Bug:** The original `extractTags(from:)` split on spaces and only kept tokens starting with `#`. This meant:

- `"shopping list,#urgent."` → split gives `["shopping", "list,#urgent."]` — `list,#urgent.` starts with `l`, not `#`, so it was dropped.
- `"(#ideas)"` → split gives `["(#ideas)"]` — starts with `(`, not `#`, so it was dropped.

**Fix:** Replaced the space-split approach with an `NSRegularExpression` matching `#(\w+)` — this finds `#` followed by word characters anywhere in the text, regardless of surrounding punctuation. Tags are returned in order of appearance, and all previously-working cases (e.g. `"hello #world #swift"`) still work because `#world` and `#swift` still match `#(\w+)`.


